B.W5=new A.dd(0,18,'This imposing domed structure is the tomb of Sir George Mackenzie, known as "Bluidy Mackenzie".')
B.VX=new A.dd(18,40,"As King's Advocate, he persecuted the Covenanters, yet was buried right beside them.")
B.VZ=new A.dd(40,65,'Since 1999, after an intruder breached the tomb, it became famous for the "Mackenzie Poltergeist".')
B.W0=new A.dd(65,95,"Hundreds of visitors have reported unexplained cold spots, scratches, and supernatural encounters here.")
B.HQ=s([B.W5,B.VX,B.VZ,B.W0],t.M3)
B.VS=new A.ko("stop-c","Stop C","Mackenzie Mausoleum","Head to the Black Mausoleum",'Follow the path to the domed mausoleum of Sir George "Bloody" Mackenzie.',"You are standing before the Black Mausoleum. Listen to the history and dark legends surrounding this tomb.","assets/audio/black_mausoleum.mp3","",null,B.It,3,'This imposing domed structure is the final resting place of Sir George Mackenzie of Rosehaugh, King\'s Advocate under Charles II.\n\nInfamous in Scottish history as "Bluidy Mackenzie," he ruthlessly persecuted the Covenanters, sending hundreds to their deaths and imprisonment just yards away. Ironically, he was buried right beside the very people he condemned.\n\nSince 1999, after a homeless intruder broke into the tomb and fell into an old pit of coffins, the mausoleum has been the epicenter of what paranormal researchers call the "Mackenzie Poltergeist" \u2014 with hundreds of documented reports of cold spots, scratches, and unexplained phenomena.',B.HQ)
